# Binary artifacts. Git must never try to diff, merge or normalise
# these, and the reproducibility check (`git status` clean after the
# pipeline) depends on their bytes being left exactly as written.
# Every pattern below is a file that already contains CRLF bytes, so
# a `text`/eol rule here would silently renormalise it and dirty the
# tree — keep them `binary`.
*.png     binary
*.mat     binary
*.db      binary
*.joblib  binary
*.ubj     binary

# Generated, not hand-written: collapse them in code review and keep
# them out of the language statistics. See the size note in
# CHANGES.md ("Repository size") — the dataset and model blobs in
# history are why `.git` is ~226 MB.
data/processed/**  linguist-generated=true
models/**          linguist-generated=true
